00:40:03.380 --> 00:40:05.500
after he goes up to the mountain

00:40:05.500 --> 00:40:06.840
Moshe

00:40:06.840 --> 00:40:09.820
Moshe comes down to earth

00:40:09.820 --> 00:40:13.920
and he tells to the people

00:40:13.920 --> 00:40:17.880
all what God had told them up in the mountain

00:40:19.880 --> 00:40:20.360
all the things

00:40:20.360 --> 00:40:22.680
all the things

00:40:22.680 --> 00:40:22.760
all the things

00:40:22.760 --> 00:40:24.160
Alright.

00:40:26.280 --> 00:40:27.100
Do you want it?

00:40:27.980 --> 00:40:28.880
This is the period.

00:40:29.860 --> 00:40:30.620
Do you want it?

00:40:31.940 --> 00:40:33.520
V'ya'an kol ha'am

00:40:33.520 --> 00:40:35.300
kol ehad.

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:37.300
In one, in unison.

00:40:37.540 --> 00:40:39.740
They say, kol abdevarim

00:40:39.740 --> 00:40:41.160
asher depel Adonai na'aseh.

00:40:42.740 --> 00:40:43.800
Are you sure

00:40:43.800 --> 00:40:44.720
you want to do it?

00:40:45.680 --> 00:40:47.440
Well, what Moshe does?

00:40:47.440 --> 00:40:49.260
V'yikhtov Moshe et kol debriyatora.

00:40:49.660 --> 00:40:50.900
Adonai. He

00:40:50.900 --> 00:40:53.100
draws a contract. He writes

00:40:53.100 --> 00:40:54.620
all the words of God.

00:40:55.840 --> 00:40:57.180
Now, it's very important.

00:40:58.080 --> 00:40:59.660
He gets up

00:40:59.660 --> 00:41:00.700
early

00:41:00.700 --> 00:41:02.820
in the next day, in the morning.

00:41:04.140 --> 00:41:04.740
Pay attention.

00:41:05.800 --> 00:41:07.600
The mountain is not

00:41:07.600 --> 00:41:08.800
trembling.

00:41:09.740 --> 00:41:10.660
There is no fire.

00:41:11.260 --> 00:41:12.260
There is no noise.

00:41:13.040 --> 00:41:15.040
There is nothing that in any way could

00:41:15.040 --> 00:41:17.140
either coerce or suggest

00:41:17.140 --> 00:41:18.340
to the Jewish people anything.

00:41:18.340 --> 00:41:19.740
God is a way

00:41:19.740 --> 00:41:21.660
they're totally free

00:41:21.660 --> 00:41:24.340
Moshe Rabbeinu draws a contract

00:41:24.340 --> 00:41:25.360
from the day before

00:41:25.360 --> 00:41:27.480
and what are the terms of the belief

00:41:27.480 --> 00:41:29.220
and

00:41:29.220 --> 00:41:31.260
Moshe Koldebi Adonai

00:41:31.260 --> 00:41:34.980
he built an altar

00:41:34.980 --> 00:41:38.520
there's 12 pillars

00:41:38.520 --> 00:41:40.680
representing

00:41:40.680 --> 00:41:42.140
symbolizing the 12 tribes

00:41:42.140 --> 00:41:48.320
and he sends the Jewish boy

00:41:48.320 --> 00:41:51.680
means the Bechorot, this used to be the Kohanim of that time.

00:41:52.580 --> 00:41:54.680
V'ya'alu'onot, they do big sacrifices.

00:41:54.860 --> 00:41:57.480
V'yizv'ahau zevachim, shenamim, davunayim,

00:41:57.740 --> 00:41:58.640
what kind of zevachim?

00:41:59.100 --> 00:42:00.040
Parim, cows.

00:42:01.220 --> 00:42:02.460
V'yikach Moshe hasi adam.

00:42:03.360 --> 00:42:06.860
Takes half of the blood and he puts it in pails.

00:42:07.680 --> 00:42:07.900
Yes?

00:42:09.240 --> 00:42:10.480
V'yazim ba'aganot.

00:42:11.360 --> 00:42:13.340
V'hasi adam, zarak ala mizbeah.

00:42:14.000 --> 00:42:16.760
In other words, God is symbolized by the mizreah.

00:42:16.760 --> 00:42:19.340
half of the blood he spills on top of the altar

00:42:19.340 --> 00:42:21.320
and half of the blood is going to

00:42:21.320 --> 00:42:23.520
spill on top of the Jewish people

00:42:23.520 --> 00:42:29.740
and before he seals the pact

00:42:29.740 --> 00:42:31.620
he takes this book of the Berit

00:42:31.620 --> 00:42:36.020
in the ears of the people

00:42:36.020 --> 00:42:38.460
do you want it?

00:42:39.780 --> 00:42:40.560
this is the deal

00:42:40.560 --> 00:42:51.180
So let's seal the deal.

00:42:52.320 --> 00:42:54.960
He takes the blood

00:42:54.960 --> 00:42:59.740
and he sprinkles over the people.

00:43:01.740 --> 00:43:03.220
And he says

00:43:03.220 --> 00:43:08.140
This is the blood of the covenant.

00:43:10.560 --> 00:43:11.960
that established the Lord.

00:43:12.700 --> 00:43:13.640
I'm with you.

00:43:14.720 --> 00:43:15.880
I'll call at the very end.

00:43:16.280 --> 00:43:17.640
Upon everything that we heard.

00:43:19.440 --> 00:43:20.640
And, alright,

00:43:20.780 --> 00:43:22.780
and then we see God,

00:43:22.960 --> 00:43:23.520
we're fine.

00:43:24.380 --> 00:43:26.080
This is the beginning of the covenant.

00:43:26.820 --> 00:43:28.440
During the rest of the 40 years,

00:43:29.120 --> 00:43:30.700
God continues giving us

00:43:30.700 --> 00:43:32.280
more Torah, a more Mesot,

00:43:32.780 --> 00:43:35.080
until we come at the end

00:43:35.080 --> 00:43:36.640
to Arbot Moab,

00:43:36.920 --> 00:43:38.180
to the valleys of Moab,

00:43:38.580 --> 00:43:40.240
before crossing the land of Israel.

00:43:40.560 --> 00:43:43.560
with the Harge Rezim and Har Ebal.

00:43:43.560 --> 00:43:46.560
And there they make another Berit.

00:43:46.560 --> 00:43:49.560
What does it mean? Another covenant means.

00:43:49.560 --> 00:43:53.560
We begin our religious history with the covenant.

00:43:53.560 --> 00:43:56.560
Misvot are given in between, then there is another covenant

00:43:56.560 --> 00:43:58.560
and that's the end of the covenant.

00:43:58.560 --> 00:44:04.560
There is no more Misvot, we don't believe no other Misva ever is going to be revealed to us

00:44:04.560 --> 00:44:05.560
and that's the law.

00:44:05.560 --> 00:44:08.560
Lotos Shev Velot Igra.

00:44:08.560 --> 00:44:10.480
We're not permitted to add to the covenant,

00:44:10.960 --> 00:44:11.740
nor to destroy,

00:44:11.960 --> 00:44:14.060
or to subtract from the covenant.

00:44:14.520 --> 00:44:16.500
And this is the basis, the constitution

00:44:16.500 --> 00:44:17.580
of the Jewish people.

00:44:18.300 --> 00:44:20.960
A covenant taken upon us

00:44:20.960 --> 00:44:22.620
and the Lord freely.

00:44:23.460 --> 00:44:24.840
A bilateral agreement.

00:44:25.400 --> 00:44:26.840
It's not a despot

00:44:26.840 --> 00:44:29.160
imposing his will

00:44:29.160 --> 00:44:30.980
upon the inferiors,

00:44:31.360 --> 00:44:32.800
but it's taken

00:44:32.800 --> 00:44:33.880
as equal

00:44:33.880 --> 00:44:36.080
between two parties.

00:44:36.080 --> 00:44:38.900
and this is the basis that's our religion

00:44:38.900 --> 00:44:40.800
basically if I go to ask you

00:44:40.800 --> 00:44:42.540
why you put tefillin

00:44:42.540 --> 00:44:43.720
you know why?

00:44:44.280 --> 00:44:45.300
you say it everyday

00:44:45.300 --> 00:44:48.340
because God made us holy

00:44:48.340 --> 00:44:49.660
how?

00:44:51.000 --> 00:44:52.500
because he ordered us

00:44:52.500 --> 00:44:53.680
to do tefillin

00:44:53.680 --> 00:44:55.940
because I want to put it in

00:44:55.940 --> 00:44:56.260
no

00:44:56.260 --> 00:45:01.440
why you put circumcision

00:45:01.440 --> 00:45:08.600
This is the covenant.

00:45:09.140 --> 00:45:10.920
Now, when we understand the covenant,

00:45:11.080 --> 00:45:13.200
we agree that that is a business, that was done.

00:45:14.680 --> 00:45:15.780
It is an eternal covenant.

00:45:17.000 --> 00:45:17.160
You see?

00:45:17.760 --> 00:45:19.020
God is going to send a Messiah.

00:45:19.200 --> 00:45:19.480
Why?

00:45:20.360 --> 00:45:21.020
You know why?

00:45:22.220 --> 00:45:24.020
Because it is that part of the covenant.

00:45:25.540 --> 00:45:26.840
That in moment of sorrows,

00:45:26.900 --> 00:45:27.800
He is going to come and save us.

00:45:27.800 --> 00:45:29.380
And ultimately, He is going to send to us

00:45:29.380 --> 00:45:31.400
the ultimate political savior.

00:45:31.440 --> 00:45:32.520
the Mashiach.

00:45:33.540 --> 00:45:35.620
What does it come with? We believe just like

00:45:35.620 --> 00:45:37.080
we observe the covenant, that's what we observe it.

00:45:37.280 --> 00:45:39.540
What happens if I don't observe the covenant tomorrow?

00:45:39.880 --> 00:45:41.620
Or we don't observe? God will punish us, but the covenant

00:45:41.620 --> 00:45:42.640
still is valid.

00:45:46.000 --> 00:45:47.260
So when God tells you,

00:45:47.320 --> 00:45:49.500
Yeshua, Muhammad, it's too young.

00:45:50.960 --> 00:45:51.580
There was no word.

00:45:51.700 --> 00:45:53.900
When God revealed himself to Muhammad in front of

00:45:53.900 --> 00:45:56.000
the hundred million Arabs?

00:45:56.460 --> 00:45:57.600
When God revealed himself

00:45:57.600 --> 00:45:59.840
to the Christians? That's in the imagination.

00:46:00.100 --> 00:46:00.280
Now,

00:46:01.440 --> 00:46:17.640
The most important thing, what I'm going to say to you now, it was the subject of an article which I published in the Jewish Court of Review about six months ago. It may sound ridiculous, but I believe it.

00:46:17.640 --> 00:46:20.440
And Harambam is our teacher in Totus.

00:46:20.600 --> 00:46:24.320
Deep question.

00:46:25.420 --> 00:46:27.040
Why tomorrow is not going to be a Harsinai?

00:46:27.160 --> 00:46:28.340
Why only once Harsinai?

00:46:30.200 --> 00:46:32.860
Harambam answers in the following.

00:46:35.800 --> 00:46:37.940
The experience of Harsinai,

00:46:38.900 --> 00:46:39.980
seeing the Lord,

00:46:40.900 --> 00:46:42.560
witnessing His voice,

00:46:43.700 --> 00:46:45.180
all the miracles there,

00:46:45.180 --> 00:46:53.420
produced such an impression upon us Jews that left its impact in the genes of the Jewish people.

00:46:53.420 --> 00:47:05.640
All of us, in our own subconscious, we have Harsinai. And therefore, our mom says it's impossible to be

00:47:05.640 --> 00:47:10.680
a genuine Jew, a Jew who's a descendant of the original Jews who stood on the mountain of Sinai,

00:47:10.680 --> 00:47:15.520
and even have a doubt about Harsinai.

00:47:16.100 --> 00:47:19.480
Because this is part of our own psychological makeup.

00:47:21.980 --> 00:47:29.700
It is the greatest experience that any human could ever have witnessed.

00:47:31.540 --> 00:47:33.100
And this is the Harsinai.

00:47:33.220 --> 00:47:33.920
That's the Matantara.

00:47:34.660 --> 00:47:37.120
In Matantara, we witnessed the Lord.

00:47:37.360 --> 00:47:38.300
That's the pension.

00:47:38.300 --> 00:47:41.140
now you want to have questions

00:47:41.140 --> 00:47:41.780
questions

00:47:41.780 --> 00:47:47.380
I tell you

00:47:47.380 --> 00:47:48.980
I believe that many of the Jews

00:47:48.980 --> 00:47:49.840
are playing games

00:47:49.840 --> 00:47:50.680
they play games

00:47:50.680 --> 00:47:55.000
they really inside their heart they believe

00:47:55.000 --> 00:47:56.480
and they are playing games

00:47:56.480 --> 00:47:58.540
I can tell you another thing

00:47:58.540 --> 00:47:59.920
I think it's their fault

00:47:59.920 --> 00:48:01.640
I think it's the fault of the training that they got

00:48:01.640 --> 00:48:02.620
they didn't get the proper

00:48:02.620 --> 00:48:04.920
genes inborn in them

00:48:04.920 --> 00:48:07.400
but it's still got to be brought out

00:48:07.400 --> 00:48:08.100
that's right

00:48:08.100 --> 00:48:10.900
it could be you have to seek there but if it's not developed

00:48:10.900 --> 00:48:11.980
it's not going to be a Jew

00:48:11.980 --> 00:48:14.800
the chain is broken

00:48:14.800 --> 00:48:16.780
somehow along the line

00:48:16.780 --> 00:48:23.440
by the way I wrote an article

00:48:23.440 --> 00:48:25.220
that was the first article I wrote in English

00:48:25.220 --> 00:48:27.000
in 1966 I published an article

00:48:27.000 --> 00:48:29.520
in a magazine

00:48:29.520 --> 00:48:30.360
called Tradition

00:48:30.360 --> 00:48:33.160
and the name of the article is Understanding the Government

00:48:33.160 --> 00:48:34.760
and there I do

00:48:34.760 --> 00:48:35.640
everything to do with the government

00:48:35.640 --> 00:48:41.880
Now, Mr. Kattan, yes, asked me a question.

00:48:43.360 --> 00:48:45.060
Well, my ancestors did the covenant.

00:48:45.160 --> 00:48:46.140
Why I have to fulfill it?

00:48:46.620 --> 00:48:46.920
All right?

00:48:47.980 --> 00:48:49.420
The answer is very simple.

00:48:50.260 --> 00:48:52.840
And it's so simple that it's worthwhile for us to know it.

00:48:53.820 --> 00:48:55.580
God make a covenant with the people of Israel.

00:48:57.000 --> 00:49:00.700
Now, if a person feels identified with the Jewish people,

00:49:01.340 --> 00:49:03.340
if you consider yourself, we consider ourselves,

00:49:03.340 --> 00:49:04.620
are the children of the Jewish people,

00:49:04.620 --> 00:49:05.780
as the Jewish people,

00:49:06.440 --> 00:49:07.020
then we have to do it.

00:49:07.040 --> 00:49:07.860
We don't want to do it.

00:49:08.300 --> 00:49:10.340
There's not even a basis for argument.

00:49:11.020 --> 00:49:11.360
In other words,

00:49:11.880 --> 00:49:13.480
once the covenant is broken,

00:49:14.400 --> 00:49:14.780
there's nothing,

00:49:14.920 --> 00:49:16.500
there's no argument,

00:49:16.680 --> 00:49:17.720
there's no rationalization,

00:49:17.880 --> 00:49:19.060
there's no philosophy in our...

00:49:19.060 --> 00:49:20.340
Either we consider ourselves

00:49:20.340 --> 00:49:22.020
as the Jewish people,

00:49:22.980 --> 00:49:23.480
or not.

00:49:23.960 --> 00:49:24.860
And you don't...

00:49:24.860 --> 00:49:26.160
No, but you just mentioned

00:49:26.160 --> 00:49:27.040
that you would be punished

00:49:27.040 --> 00:49:29.120
if you did not fulfill the covenant.

00:49:29.860 --> 00:49:30.600
This I believe.

00:49:31.100 --> 00:49:31.580
But that doesn't mean

00:49:31.580 --> 00:49:32.500
because I believe

00:49:32.500 --> 00:49:32.980
that's very...

00:49:32.980 --> 00:49:33.980
I don't believe.

00:49:34.060 --> 00:49:34.520
I don't believe.

00:49:34.620 --> 00:49:39.120
But in other words, the basis for argument is the acceptance of the covenant.

00:49:39.720 --> 00:49:42.260
If a person does not accept the covenant, there's nothing to speak with that person.

00:49:43.560 --> 00:49:45.500
The bridge is broken.

00:49:46.960 --> 00:49:50.460
In other words, we could argue with each other as long as we accept the covenant.

00:49:51.060 --> 00:49:52.000
What about the search?

00:49:52.200 --> 00:49:52.720
Which search?

00:49:53.600 --> 00:49:55.080
The person that searched.

00:49:57.260 --> 00:49:59.720
Well, what Hakan David said before,

00:49:59.720 --> 00:50:03.720
and today, unfortunately, sometimes the search is a result of poor leadership.

00:50:04.620 --> 00:50:06.520
if a person wants to search, I think that

00:50:06.520 --> 00:50:08.000
person is very worthwhile.

00:50:08.500 --> 00:50:10.420
He should search, but the point is

00:50:10.420 --> 00:50:12.860
as long as the person is outside the covenant,

00:50:12.920 --> 00:50:14.280
if a person says, I don't accept the covenant,

00:50:15.060 --> 00:50:17.120
then there's nothing to argue with him.

00:50:17.380 --> 00:50:18.620
Why not bring him back in?

00:50:19.320 --> 00:50:20.240
Because, this is the point,

00:50:20.500 --> 00:50:22.100
you could bring only somebody through reason,

00:50:22.680 --> 00:50:24.260
but the basis of our Torah

00:50:24.260 --> 00:50:26.340
is not our reason, but rather

00:50:26.340 --> 00:50:27.680
the covenant itself.

00:50:29.260 --> 00:50:30.700
In other words, reason is not

00:50:30.700 --> 00:50:31.540
stronger than the covenant.

00:50:31.540 --> 00:50:33.980
the strong thing is the covenant

00:50:33.980 --> 00:50:35.900
that we make with God, the Berit.

00:50:37.160 --> 00:50:37.420
You see?

00:50:38.080 --> 00:50:38.980
Yeah, but of the men.

00:50:39.080 --> 00:50:41.760
One of the ways that we call the servant is Bene Berit,

00:50:41.860 --> 00:50:42.940
the children of the Berit,

00:50:43.660 --> 00:50:44.660
the children of the pact.

00:50:44.960 --> 00:50:48.020
But the man has doubts. Does that mean that he's true?

00:50:48.720 --> 00:50:49.040
No.

00:50:49.240 --> 00:50:50.660
I say that's a good man.

00:50:51.460 --> 00:50:53.700
But as long as a person has doubts

00:50:53.700 --> 00:50:56.600
about the actual Berit,

00:50:57.860 --> 00:50:58.420
there's nothing

00:50:58.420 --> 00:50:59.520
that can be done.

00:50:59.520 --> 00:51:00.820
That's not going to exist.

00:51:00.820 --> 00:51:04.220
Perhaps. Maybe that happens.

00:51:05.080 --> 00:51:07.100
Let's say there's no doubt, right?

00:51:07.900 --> 00:51:10.800
But see, we base everything today on logic.

00:51:12.520 --> 00:51:18.040
Now, the idea is that a lot of things that haven't been given to us are logical.

00:51:19.080 --> 00:51:27.560
But the biggest certainty is that our mentality hasn't been able to reach to find out the logic to it.

00:51:27.760 --> 00:51:29.140
Because there is a logic to it.

00:51:29.140 --> 00:51:32.440
The fact that you can't understand it doesn't allow you to doubt.

00:51:32.640 --> 00:51:33.380
Yeah, but...

00:51:33.380 --> 00:51:34.560
It doesn't allow you to doubt.

00:51:35.260 --> 00:51:37.100
Yeah, but there is a logical...

00:51:37.100 --> 00:51:38.440
There is a logical point.

00:51:38.780 --> 00:51:40.020
Well, there is a logical point.

00:51:41.020 --> 00:51:41.460
Exactly.

00:51:42.080 --> 00:51:45.160
In the beginning, we begin with emunah.

00:51:45.920 --> 00:51:47.440
I mean, it's an act of faith.

00:51:48.100 --> 00:51:50.540
The fact that someone can't explain it to you, you're not...

00:51:50.540 --> 00:51:52.040
No, no, no, no, I'm not saying that.

00:51:52.040 --> 00:51:52.880
What did you understand?

00:51:53.200 --> 00:51:53.720
No logical.

00:51:54.200 --> 00:51:54.380
No.

00:51:54.600 --> 00:51:56.480
It's not logical, you have to believe it.

00:51:56.980 --> 00:51:57.340
No, no.

00:51:57.340 --> 00:52:00.100
What he's saying, I mean, both are correct.

00:52:01.100 --> 00:52:02.960
Because everything has a logic.

00:52:05.880 --> 00:52:07.680
Let's take an example of pork.

00:52:08.700 --> 00:52:10.160
So suppose a person would say,

00:52:11.080 --> 00:52:13.140
well, I don't eat pork because it's unhealthy.

00:52:14.420 --> 00:52:17.220
Now, from the point of view of the fact, it's like this.

00:52:18.740 --> 00:52:20.960
I don't eat the pork because this is a covenant.

00:52:21.480 --> 00:52:25.380
It happened to be that I happen to believe at the same time

00:52:25.380 --> 00:52:27.100
that it's unhealthy.

00:52:27.340 --> 00:52:29.140
But that is a secondary reason.

00:52:29.300 --> 00:52:31.220
You know, it is a rationalization.

00:52:31.440 --> 00:52:33.460
We believe, that is the point of Haramban.

00:52:34.020 --> 00:52:37.240
Haramban believes that every muswa has a ta'am.

00:52:38.100 --> 00:52:40.220
But the reason why we don't is not a ta'am.

00:52:40.720 --> 00:52:42.220
We do it because it's a covenant.

00:52:43.140 --> 00:52:43.440
You see?

00:52:44.160 --> 00:52:45.140
It's a circumcision.

00:52:45.540 --> 00:52:47.220
Haramban believes that circumcision is very healthy.

00:52:47.660 --> 00:52:49.740
But we don't do circumcision because of the health.

00:52:49.880 --> 00:52:51.740
We do it because God commanded us.

00:52:52.200 --> 00:52:54.040
It happened to be...

00:52:54.040 --> 00:52:56.120
Now, I want to...

00:52:56.120 --> 00:52:57.200
Do we have a minute or two?

00:52:57.340 --> 00:52:58.700
Yeah, we do have some time.

00:52:59.460 --> 00:52:59.600
Right?

00:53:00.580 --> 00:53:03.180
I was going to read to you the Ten Commandments.

00:53:03.460 --> 00:53:04.520
We didn't have a chance to read it.

00:53:04.620 --> 00:53:05.200
You know it.

00:53:05.280 --> 00:53:06.100
You don't have to tell me.

00:53:06.100 --> 00:53:07.260
You don't need me to tell you.

00:53:07.460 --> 00:53:09.600
But I want to tell you just one thing about the Ten Commandments,

00:53:09.660 --> 00:53:10.600
which I think is beautiful.

00:53:11.260 --> 00:53:13.240
And I read it in the B'yir Yahub Ben Amozek.

00:53:13.580 --> 00:53:14.600
And I think you'll love it.

00:53:15.380 --> 00:53:16.120
It says like this.

00:53:17.080 --> 00:53:18.440
Zahor Yitom HaShabbat Yikad Esho.

00:53:19.980 --> 00:53:21.620
Remember the Yom Shabbat and make it holy.

00:53:22.160 --> 00:53:23.200
Or declare it sacred.

00:53:23.920 --> 00:53:24.120
Yes.

00:53:24.880 --> 00:53:25.660
Kishesh Yit Yamim.

00:53:25.720 --> 00:53:26.880
Asad V'Namit HaShomim V'taharis.

00:53:27.340 --> 00:53:29.420
not see the reason, why you have to celebrate the Shabbat?

00:53:30.160 --> 00:53:31.160
Because God worked for

00:53:31.160 --> 00:53:31.940
six days,

00:53:33.440 --> 00:53:34.760
and we almost

00:53:34.760 --> 00:53:36.620
and he rested in the Sabbath.

00:53:37.440 --> 00:53:38.180
So listen to this.

00:53:39.560 --> 00:53:40.900
Yeah, no, that's not the

00:53:40.900 --> 00:53:42.600
thing. A different question.

00:53:43.460 --> 00:53:44.320
This is strange.

00:53:45.540 --> 00:53:46.820
We celebrate

00:53:46.820 --> 00:53:49.120
not the creation of the universe,

00:53:50.080 --> 00:53:51.020
but the fact that

00:53:51.020 --> 00:53:51.680
God rested.

00:53:53.020 --> 00:53:55.100
So instead of Shabbat should be the first

00:53:55.100 --> 00:53:56.700
day. Sunday should be the celebration,

00:53:56.700 --> 00:54:00.140
Because if you give Yom Rishon, God will begin to work.

00:54:01.480 --> 00:54:02.780
I mean, what is more important?

00:54:03.560 --> 00:54:07.040
The beginning of the creation or the fact that God stopped working?

00:54:09.540 --> 00:54:12.200
Should be logic to say beginning of creation.

00:54:13.200 --> 00:54:15.520
The Yom Rishon is supposed to be the most important day.

00:54:16.540 --> 00:54:17.680
Or the sixth day.

00:54:18.020 --> 00:54:18.680
But not the seventh.

00:54:18.760 --> 00:54:19.760
The seventh didn't do anything.

00:54:22.060 --> 00:54:22.760
Do you understand the question?

00:54:25.240 --> 00:54:25.800
All right?

00:54:25.800 --> 00:54:31.900
the answer is really, you and I understand that you see some of the

00:54:31.900 --> 00:54:43.460
depth of our Torah. Suppose we have nature. Now one of the things that we

00:54:43.460 --> 00:54:50.660
know in nature, suppose I don't know I take a ball and I throw it into a vacuum.

00:54:50.660 --> 00:55:00.660
This ball will continue forever into the vacuum, going until something stronger makes it stop.

00:55:00.660 --> 00:55:04.660
Correct? This is simple. That's all in nature.

00:55:04.660 --> 00:55:10.660
You need some resistance. If there is no resistance, things continue doing exactly the way they are.

00:55:10.660 --> 00:55:12.660
It's inertia.

00:55:12.660 --> 00:55:14.660
You see, it's unbelievable.

00:55:14.660 --> 00:55:20.660
Now, that is the greatness of Yom Shabbat.

00:55:20.660 --> 00:55:29.660
That God created the universe, all the Goyim says that there is a God or some God or nature or whatever it is that created the universe.

00:55:29.660 --> 00:55:34.660
But that nature, that power, it never stops.

00:55:34.660 --> 00:55:38.660
It never stops. Nature never stops.

00:55:38.660 --> 00:55:45.360
So therefore that nature is not different than the world itself that it created.

00:55:45.360 --> 00:55:48.060
It has no control over itself.

00:55:48.060 --> 00:55:52.040
The greatness of God from the Jewish point of view is not that he start creating the

00:55:52.040 --> 00:55:54.680
world but he could stop.

00:55:54.680 --> 00:55:56.420
You see?

00:55:56.420 --> 00:55:59.920
Only God could stop.

00:55:59.920 --> 00:56:04.260
Other people they conceive a nature but the nature that the scientists conceive is a nature

00:56:04.260 --> 00:56:07.500
that could begin but never could stop.

00:56:07.500 --> 00:56:11.500
What we conceive is something that could stop.

00:56:11.500 --> 00:56:15.500
And therefore we celebrate Kiyom HaSharei Shabbat.

00:56:15.500 --> 00:56:19.500
But we celebrate the fact that He has the power to stop.

00:56:19.500 --> 00:56:23.500
That is deep.

00:56:23.500 --> 00:56:27.500
Alright? Now, shall we say Kaddish?

00:56:27.500 --> 00:56:29.500
Yes, yes, yes.

00:56:29.500 --> 00:56:33.500
I've been watching this show and folks, I gotta tell you, I'm getting a kick out of it.

00:56:33.500 --> 00:56:35.980
I just got back from a pleasure trip.

00:56:36.220 --> 00:56:37.400
Took my mother all to the airport.

00:56:43.940 --> 00:56:45.420
Man walks into a psychiatrist.

00:56:45.620 --> 00:56:46.500
Says, nobody talks to me.

00:56:46.580 --> 00:56:46.920
Says, next.

00:56:50.820 --> 00:56:52.500
Another fellow walks into a psychiatrist.

00:56:52.900 --> 00:56:53.720
He says, you're crazy.

00:56:54.040 --> 00:56:55.000
Says, I want a second opinion.

00:56:55.220 --> 00:56:55.960
You're ugly, too.

00:56:57.520 --> 00:56:58.600
I'm on this crowd.

00:56:58.600 --> 00:57:04.600
They put a priest up in Alaska.

00:57:04.780 --> 00:57:05.440
He's there for a year.

00:57:05.740 --> 00:57:06.880
The bishop comes up to visit.

00:57:06.980 --> 00:57:07.900
We said, how do you like it here?

00:57:08.220 --> 00:57:10.060
He said, if it wasn't for my rosary

00:57:10.060 --> 00:57:11.720
and my two martinis a day,

00:57:11.760 --> 00:57:12.780
I couldn't stand it here.

00:57:13.400 --> 00:57:14.420
He said to the bishop,

00:57:14.500 --> 00:57:15.360
will you like a martini?

00:57:15.460 --> 00:57:16.220
He said, yeah, rosary.

00:57:16.440 --> 00:57:17.400
Get the bishop a martini.

00:57:25.400 --> 00:57:26.920
I went to a doctor myself.

00:57:27.260 --> 00:57:28.080
He says, you're pregnant.

00:57:28.600 --> 00:57:31.640
I said, how does a man get pregnant?

00:57:31.860 --> 00:57:33.840
She said, usually a little dinner, a little wine.

00:57:37.580 --> 00:57:39.220
Two dumb guys are walking along.

00:57:39.520 --> 00:57:40.520
One says, look at a dead bird.

00:57:40.600 --> 00:57:41.260
He says, where, where?

00:57:50.780 --> 00:57:52.940
During the blackout, you know you had a blackout,

00:57:53.020 --> 00:57:54.440
and the fellow's walking along with his girlfriend.

00:57:54.600 --> 00:57:55.720
He says, I'll get you anything you want.

00:57:56.360 --> 00:57:57.960
She says, I want that perm coat.

00:57:57.960 --> 00:57:59.060
He throws a brick through the window.

00:57:59.600 --> 00:58:00.960
Now she says, I want that motorcycle.

00:58:01.860 --> 00:58:02.840
Throws a brick through the window.

00:58:03.000 --> 00:58:04.200
Now she wants that big diamond.

00:58:04.480 --> 00:58:05.980
He says, what do you think I am, paid out of bricks?

00:58:09.920 --> 00:58:11.420
I got a wonderful doctor post.

00:58:11.500 --> 00:58:12.580
Gave him that six months to live.

00:58:12.660 --> 00:58:13.260
Couldn't pay his bill.

00:58:13.340 --> 00:58:14.120
Gave him another six months.

00:58:20.100 --> 00:58:21.400
Sometimes I had to walk in the morning.

00:58:21.540 --> 00:58:22.260
I got burned faces.

00:58:22.400 --> 00:58:22.740
What happened?

00:58:23.220 --> 00:58:24.720
They were bobbing for French fries.

00:58:27.960 --> 00:58:29.980
I want to do a song now, folks,

00:58:30.040 --> 00:58:31.920
because I've been asked to do a little fiddle playing tonight.

00:58:32.160 --> 00:58:35.060
And a lot of people ask me,

00:58:35.400 --> 00:58:36.560
do you know anything about music?

00:58:36.640 --> 00:58:37.540
Well, I know one thing.

00:58:37.660 --> 00:58:40.120
That when Lubbock, von Beethoven, the great composer,

00:58:40.540 --> 00:58:42.940
was about 19 years old, he couldn't write anymore.

00:58:43.040 --> 00:58:43.640
He went bad.

00:58:43.840 --> 00:58:44.840
He was drinking a lot.

00:58:45.260 --> 00:58:47.540
He looked disheveled, and his wife threatened to leave him.

00:58:47.860 --> 00:58:49.120
He said, don't leave me, don't leave me.

00:58:49.140 --> 00:58:50.080
I love you, I love you.

00:58:50.080 --> 00:58:51.120
She said, you love me.

00:58:51.320 --> 00:58:52.080
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

00:58:57.960 --> 00:59:27.940
Thank you.

00:59:27.960 --> 00:59:30.560
You know what's embarrassing?

00:59:30.700 --> 00:59:32.400
When you look through a keyhole, you see another eye.

00:59:37.200 --> 00:59:38.200
Take the last eight.

00:59:46.780 --> 00:59:49.680
Folks, it's a pleasure being here with my buddy Chuck Barris,

00:59:49.740 --> 00:59:50.880
and I'm glad he's doing so well.

00:59:50.920 --> 00:59:51.940
He's a real grand guy.

00:59:57.960 --> 01:00:27.940
Thank you.

